From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LIVI appliance
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 20:10:00 +1030
Subject: [PATCH] soc: sunxi: sram: add the H616 VE SRAM section

cedrus claims the video engine's SRAM through the allwinner,sram
phandle before it probes, so the video-codec node added in 0003 needs a
section the SRAM driver knows. The H616 control register layout is the
one mainline added for the SoC (master's sun50i_h616_ve_sram: bit 0 of
the system control register, 1 = CPU, 0 = VE), not the H6's 31-bit C1
window; backport that descriptor and its compatible.

The H616 system control node is already matched by this driver's
sun50i_h616_sramc_variant, so only the section entry is new.
---
 drivers/soc/sunxi/sunxi_sram.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/soc/sunxi/sunxi_sram.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/sunxi/sunxi_sram.c
@@ -81,6 +81,12 @@
 				  SUNXI_SRAM_MAP(0, 1, "de2")),
 };
 
+static struct sunxi_sram_desc sun50i_h616_ve_sram = {
+	.data	= SUNXI_SRAM_DATA("VE", 0x0, 0, 1,
+				  SUNXI_SRAM_MAP(1, 0, "cpu"),
+				  SUNXI_SRAM_MAP(0, 1, "ve")),
+};
+
 static const struct of_device_id sunxi_sram_dt_ids[] = {
 	{
 		.compatible	= "allwinner,sun4i-a10-sram-a3-a4",
@@ -98,6 +104,10 @@
 		.compatible	= "allwinner,sun50i-a64-sram-c",
 		.data		= &sun50i_a64_sram_c.data,
 	},
+	{
+		.compatible	= "allwinner,sun50i-h616-ve-sram",
+		.data		= &sun50i_h616_ve_sram.data,
+	},
 	{}
 };
 
